#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059482 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059653 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f372d875-4de9-5ed1-86a6-80ceeddd3fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of a Triangle's Side Using the Law of Cosines"}] :question/id #uuid "0383d558-2227-5c47-b0d3-8ac48c7b1e7a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3286" :question/problem "Consider the following triangle:\n\n![](images/9f/9fbf9672296b128a16336120999c2c836d950fda32154bc7a0f0a91b0e8799e6.png)\n\nCalculate the length of the side $a$, giving your answer to the nearest tenth." :question/worked-solution "The Law of Cosines states that\n\n$$\na^2 = b^2+c^2-2bc\\cos{A}\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nm\\angle A = 75^{\\circ},\\quad b = 10,\\quad c=9\n$$\n\nSubstituting the numbers into the formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na^{2} &= 10^{2} + 9^{2} - 2(10)(9)\\cos 75^{∘} \\\\\n&= 100 + 81 - 180\\cos 75^{∘} \\\\\n&= 181 - 180 \\cdot 0.2588… \\\\\n&= 181 - 46.5874… \\\\\n&= 134.4126\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places\n\nTaking the square root gives\n\n$$\na = \\sqrt{134.4126} = 11.6\n$$\n\nto the nearest tenth."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059483 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8da5ae4c-c94c-5a8c-ba62-5df6e500008a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Measure of an Angle in a Triangle Using the Law of Cosines"}] :question/id #uuid "84630f24-0d62-5ab3-8f9d-e03e815820cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-3288" :question/problem "Consider the following triangle:\n\n![](images/e0/e03942073ddfd8672fe5c5e4bd7bc81f0dc22f8682e3a364b001c280b315e721.png)\n\nCalculate the measure of the angle $\\angle A$ to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "We use the Law of Cosines to solve for angle $A$:\n\n$$\n\\cos A = \\frac{b^{2} + c^{2} - a^{2}}{2bc}\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\na=9,\\quad b=7,\\quad c=12\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos A &= (7^{2} + 12^{2} - 9^{2})/(2(7)(12)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{49 + 144 - 81}{168} \\\\\n&= \\frac{112}{168} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠A &= \\arccos (\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\\n&= 48.19^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto two decimal places."}]}
